anner in","kjv":"a standard"}},{"chapterId":"ezk-27","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"banner","kjv":"to be thy sail"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Exodus 17:15","note":"Moses built an altar, and called its name “Yahweh our Banner”.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Numbers 21:8","note":"Yahweh said to Moses, “Make a venomous snake, and set it on a pole. It shall happen that everyone who is bitten, when he sees it, shall live.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 60:4","note":"You have given a banner to those who fear you, that it may be displayed because of the truth.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 5:26","note":"He will lift up a banner to the nations from far away, and he will whistle for them from the end of the earth. Behold, they will come speedily and swiftly.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Jeremiah 4:6","note":"Set up a standard toward Zion. Flee for safety! Don’t wait; for I will bring evil from the north, and a great destruction.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"Ezekiel 27:7","note":"Your sail was of fine linen with embroidered work from Egypt, that it might be to you for a banner. Blue and purple from the islands of Elishah was your awning.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H3068","lemma":"יְהֹוָה","transliteration":"yehovah","gloss":"LORD"},{"id":"H3071","lemma":"יְהֹוָה נִסִּי","transliteration":"yehovah nissi","gloss":"YHWH/Jehovah-nissi"}],"senses":[{"id":"H5251H","gloss":"ensign","relation":"H5251H ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}